%[text] # BC121 Configuration A: mesh convergence of the FEA results
%[text] **J.G. Vermond, JVsound**
%[text] Prepared on 2026-10-15. This script checks whether the Ansys Mechanical results of configuration A (one cabinet lying, flat diaphragm) are reliable. The same harmonic acoustics analysis was solved with three global mesh sizes. The results are reliable when a finer mesh no longer changes them: the difference between the two finest meshes must stay below `tolerance`. Three quantities are compared: the averaged pressure on the front and the rear of the diaphragm, the SPL at 1 m (a microphone in the mesh) and the SPL at the microphones outside the mesh at 5 and 10 m.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Contents"}
%[text] - pressure on the diaphragm (`diaf` and `diar`) due to the imposed velocity of 1 mm/s
%[text] - the SPL of the loudspeaker system, calculated with the FEA enclosure at 28.3 V RMS
%[text] - SPL at 1 m in the mesh domain
%[text] - SPL at 5 and 10 m outside the mesh domain
%[text] - summary of the differences between the meshes \
%%
%[text] ## Settings
%[text] The meshes are listed from coarse to fine; only the meshes with exports in `Simulation\MeshStudy\<size> mm\` are used, so the script also runs while a mesh is still being solved. Every folder holds the exports of Mechanical (in MPa): `Average Pressure Diaphragm Front.txt`, `Average Pressure Diaphragm Rear.txt` and `Pressure Mic1m.txt` (columns Frequency, Amplitude, Phase Angle, Real, Imaginary), and per far-field microphone `Far-field Maximum Pressure Mic<distance>m.txt` and `Far-field Phase Mic<distance>m.txt`.
meshSizes = [200 175 150]; % Global mesh size in [mm], coarse to fine
micDistances = [5 10]; % Far-field microphones outside the mesh in [m]
tolerance = 1; % Allowed SPL difference between the two finest meshes in [dB]
exportFolder = fullfile(currentProject().RootFolder,"Simulation","MeshStudy");
sourceVoltage = 28.3; % RMS voltage of the amplifier in [V]
diaphragmVelocity = 1e-3; % Velocity imposed on the diaphragm in the FEA model in [m/s]
pRef = 20e-6; % Reference pressure for the SPL in [Pa]
hasExport = arrayfun(@(s) isfile(fullfile(exportFolder,s + " mm","Pressure Mic1m.txt")),meshSizes);
meshSizes = meshSizes(hasExport);
meshLabels = meshSizes + " mm";
micNames = micDistances + " m";
numMesh = numel(meshSizes);
numMic = numel(micDistances);
%%
%[text] ## Read the FEA results
%[text] The complex pressure is the real and the imaginary part of the export, converted from MPa to Pa. The pressure of a far-field microphone comes from `readFarField`, which reads the amplitude and the phase files of the folder and returns the complex pressure. All meshes must have the same frequencies, otherwise the differences cannot be taken.
readExport = @(file) readmatrix(file,FileType="text",NumHeaderLines=1);
pFront = []; pRear = []; pMeshMic = []; pFarMic = cell(1,numMic);
for m = 1:numMesh
    folder = fullfile(exportFolder,meshSizes(m) + " mm");
    front = readExport(fullfile(folder,"Average Pressure Diaphragm Front.txt"));
    rear = readExport(fullfile(folder,"Average Pressure Diaphragm Rear.txt"));
    mesh1m = readExport(fullfile(folder,"Pressure Mic1m.txt"));
    if m == 1
        frequency = front(:,1);
    end
    sameFrequency = @(x) size(x,1) == numel(frequency) && max(abs(x(:,1) - frequency)) < 1e-3*max(frequency);
    assert(sameFrequency(front) && sameFrequency(rear) && sameFrequency(mesh1m), ...
        "Mesh %g mm has other frequencies than mesh %g mm.",meshSizes(m),meshSizes(1))
    pFront(:,m) = (front(:,4) + 1i*front(:,5))*1e6; %#ok<SAGROW>
    pRear(:,m) = (rear(:,4) + 1i*rear(:,5))*1e6; %#ok<SAGROW>
    pMeshMic(:,m) = (mesh1m(:,4) + 1i*mesh1m(:,5))*1e6; %#ok<SAGROW>
    farField = readFarField(folder,"Mic" + micDistances + "m");
    for k = 1:numMic
        assert(sameFrequency([farField(k).Frequency.' farField(k).Frequency.']), ...
            "Microphone %s of mesh %g mm has other frequencies.",micNames(k),meshSizes(m))
        pFarMic{k}(:,m) = farField(k).Pressure.';
    end
end
disp("Meshes read: " + join(meshLabels,", ")) %[output:5baad668]
%[text] The difference of a mesh is taken against the finest mesh, so it is zero for the last column. `spl` is only used to express the diaphragm pressure as a level in the summary, from the RMS value, so the amplitude divided by $ \\sqrt{2} $.
spl = @(p) 20*log10(abs(p)/sqrt(2)/pRef);
diffFinest = @(x) x - x(:,end);
splUnit = "dB re 20 " + char(181) + "Pa";
%%
%[text] ## Pressure on the front of the diaphragm
%[text] Magnitude of the pressure averaged over `diaf` (amplitude in Pa) for the imposed velocity of 1 mm/s, and the difference of the coarser meshes with the finest mesh. The front is the side that loads the horn, so it is the most sensitive to the mesh.
tiledlayout(2,1) %[output:47bef81a]
nexttile %[output:47bef81a]
loglog(frequency,abs(pFront)), grid on %[output:47bef81a]
ylabel("Pressure (Pa)"), legend(meshLabels,Location="best"), title("Front of the diaphragm (diaf)") %[output:47bef81a]
nexttile %[output:47bef81a]
semilogx(frequency,diffFinest(abs(pFront))), grid on %[output:47bef81a]
xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (Pa)"), title("Difference with the finest mesh") %[output:47bef81a]
%%
%[text] ## Pressure on the rear of the diaphragm
%[text] The rear radiates into the closed rear chamber (about 109 L). It is expected to be nearly independent of the mesh, as in the earlier tests, and different from the front.
tiledlayout(2,1) %[output:7851f147]
nexttile %[output:7851f147]
loglog(frequency,abs(pRear)), grid on %[output:7851f147]
ylabel("Pressure (Pa)"), legend(meshLabels,Location="best"), title("Rear of the diaphragm (diar)") %[output:7851f147]
nexttile %[output:7851f147]
semilogx(frequency,diffFinest(abs(pRear))), grid on %[output:7851f147]
xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (Pa)"), title("Difference with the finest mesh") %[output:7851f147]
%[text] Check on the exports: the front and the rear of the diaphragm must differ.
frontEqualsRear = max(abs(pFront - pRear),[],"all") < 1e-6*max(abs(pFront),[],"all") %[output:120b69b3]
%%
%[text] ## Calculate the SPL with the loudspeaker system
%[text] The SPL at a microphone is calculated per mesh with an `lspsys` that has a `comp.FeaEnclosure` and the B&C 21SW152-8 as driver, driven with `sourceVoltage` (RMS). The enclosure gets the averaged pressure on the front and the rear of the diaphragm of that mesh, which give the loads of the horn and of the closed rear chamber. The pressure at the microphone, in the mesh (1 m) or outside it (5 and 10 m), is the transfer of the FEA model times the volume velocity of the system. `diaphragmVelocity` must be the velocity that the FEA model imposes on the projected area of the cone.
splMesh1m = zeros(numel(frequency),numMesh);
splFarMic = repmat({zeros(numel(frequency),numMesh)},1,numMic);
asData = @(p) struct(Frequency=frequency.',Pressure=p.');
for m = 1:numMesh
    sys = lspsys;
    sys.SourceVoltage = sourceVoltage;
    sys.Enclosure = comp.FeaEnclosure;
    sys.Enclosure.PressureFront = asData(pFront(:,m));
    sys.Enclosure.PressureRear = asData(pRear(:,m));
    sys.Enclosure.DiaphragmVelocity = diaphragmVelocity;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver = comp.Driver;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Re = 6;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Le = 2.2e-3;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Qes = 0.38;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Qms = 6.4;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Fs = 32;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Sd = 1680e-4;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Vas = 200e-3;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Znom = 8;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Zmin = 7;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Pnom = 2000;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Xvar = 16e-3;
    sys.Frequency = sys.Enclosure.Frequency;
    sys.Enclosure.PressureFarField = asData(pMeshMic(:,m));
    res = sys.createResult;
    splMesh1m(:,m) = res.SoundPressureLevel(:);
    for k = 1:numMic
        sys.Enclosure.PressureFarField = asData(pFarMic{k}(:,m));
        res = sys.createResult;
        splFarMic{k}(:,m) = res.SoundPressureLevel(:);
    end
end
%%
%[text] ## SPL at 1 m (in the mesh domain)
%[text] The SPL at the microphone in the mesh, on the floor 1 m from the mouth of the horn, at the source voltage.
tiledlayout(2,1) %[output:53b108ae]
nexttile %[output:53b108ae]
semilogx(frequency,splMesh1m), grid on %[output:53b108ae]
ylabel(splUnit), legend(meshLabels,Location="best"), title("Microphone at 1 m") %[output:53b108ae]
nexttile %[output:53b108ae]
semilogx(frequency,diffFinest(splMesh1m)), grid on %[output:53b108ae]
yline([-tolerance tolerance],"--k",HandleVisibility="off") %[output:53b108ae]
xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (dB)"), title("Difference with the finest mesh") %[output:53b108ae]
%%
%[text] ## SPL at 5 and 10 m (outside the mesh domain)
%[text] The far-field microphones are calculated from the surface of the mesh domain. Their level depends on the mesh through the pressure on that surface. Top: the SPL, bottom: the difference with the finest mesh, with the tolerance as dashed lines.
tiledlayout(2,numMic) %[output:34cd76e7]
for k = 1:numMic %[output:group:02f6380c]
    nexttile(k) %[output:34cd76e7]
    semilogx(frequency,splFarMic{k}), grid on
    title("Microphone at " + micNames(k)), ylabel(splUnit)
    if k == 1
        legend(meshLabels,Location="best")
    end
    nexttile(numMic + k)
    semilogx(frequency,diffFinest(splFarMic{k})), grid on
    yline([-tolerance tolerance],"--k",HandleVisibility="off")
    xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (dB)")
end %[output:group:02f6380c]
%%
%[text] ## Summary
%[text] Maximum and RMS difference over all frequencies of the coarser meshes with the finest mesh, and whether the second finest mesh is within `tolerance`. The microphones are compared as the SPL of the loudspeaker system at `sourceVoltage`; the diaphragm pressure is compared as a level, so its difference is the ratio of the pressures in dB.
quantity = ["Front diaphragm" "Rear diaphragm" "Mic 1 m" "Mic " + micNames].';
levels = {spl(pFront) spl(pRear) splMesh1m};
for k = 1:numMic
    levels{end+1} = splFarMic{k}; %#ok<SAGROW>
end
summary = table(quantity,VariableNames="Quantity");
for m = 1:numMesh-1
    summary.("Max " + meshSizes(m) + " mm") = cellfun(@(x) max(abs(x(:,m) - x(:,end))),levels).';
    summary.("RMS " + meshSizes(m) + " mm") = cellfun(@(x) sqrt(mean((x(:,m) - x(:,end)).^2)),levels).';
end
%[text] The results are reliable for the quantities with `Converged` true. For the others, a finer mesh is needed or the mesh on the diaphragm and in the horn must be refined locally.
if numMesh > 1 %[output:group:3c096d23]
    summary.Converged = summary.("Max " + meshSizes(end-1) + " mm") < tolerance;
    disp(summary) %[output:04b0abe8]
else
    disp("Only one mesh (" + meshLabels + ") has exports: no comparison yet.")
end %[output:group:3c096d23]

